@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home - Child Care Licensing</PageTitle>

<h1>Child care licensing and compliance</h1>

<p class="lead">
    A demo portal for licensing child care centres. Operators register a facility, have room
    capacity checked against provincial-style rules, and submit an application for review.
    Ministry staff track compliance risk, and the public can look up any licensed centre.
</p>

<section aria-labelledby="quick-start-heading">
    <h2 id="quick-start-heading">Try it</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Open <a href="/facilities">My facilities</a> and pick a centre.</li>
        <li>Review the rooms and run capacity validation against the ratio and floor-area rules.</li>
        <li>Submit the application once every room passes.</li>
        <li>Check the <a href="/reports">compliance reports</a> and the <a href="/registry">public register</a>.</li>
    </ol>

    <a class="button" href="/facilities/22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222/application">
        Open the sample application
    </a>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <h2 id="how-heading">How it is built</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>ASP.NET Core Web API and Blazor Server on .NET 10, in a layered solution.</li>
        <li>The capacity rules engine lives in the domain layer with no infrastructure dependencies.</li>
        <li>EF Core handles transactional work; Dapper and stored procedures handle reporting.</li>
        <li>A background worker expires licences, issues renewal notices and escalates overdue findings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        API documentation is available at <a href="/openapi/v1.json">/openapi/v1.json</a> and the
        health probe at <a href="/health">/health</a>.
    </p>
</section>
